# AGENTS.md — the contract for every coding agent

**This file is the single source of truth for how work is done in this repository.** Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini, Copilot, Antigravity, and any human all follow the same rules. `CLAUDE.md` defers to this file; if the two ever disagree, this file wins and `CLAUDE.md` must be corrected.

Picking up mid-task? Read [STATUS.md](STATUS.md) first.

Canonical links: [Product Spec](docs/product-spec.md) · [Spec Changelog](docs/spec-changelog.md) · [Changelog](CHANGELOG.md) · [Roadmap](docs/roadmap.md)

---

## 1. The Definition of Done

### 1.1 Always required
- [ ] The project's verification command passes (tests + typecheck/build — replace with this repo's actual command, e.g. `npm run verify` or `xcodebuild test -scheme ... `).
- [ ] A test exists for the behavior that changed, where the codebase's existing testing convention makes that practical.
- [ ] `CHANGELOG.md`'s `## [Unreleased]` section has a one-line, user-visible-effect entry for the change.
- [ ] `STATUS.md` reflects the current state of the work — updated in the same session, not as an afterthought.

### 1.2 Required when the change is user-visible or architectural
- [ ] Snapshot the current spec: `./scripts/bump-spec.sh snapshot` (or manually `cp docs/product-spec.md docs/specs/product-spec-v<CURRENT>.md`).
- [ ] Bump the version header in `docs/product-spec.md` and its `Historical versions` line.
- [ ] Update the relevant spec section(s) with the new behavior.
- [ ] Add an entry to the top of `docs/spec-changelog.md` naming the changed sections.
- [ ] Save the new snapshot: `./scripts/bump-spec.sh save` (or manually `cp docs/product-spec.md docs/specs/product-spec-v<NEW>.md`).

### 1.3 Required when you add a migration
- [ ] Migrations are additive/immutable once merged — never edit a migration that's already shipped; write a new one.
- [ ] [Fill in this repo's actual migration tooling/commands.]

### 1.4 Required when you change a rule in this file
- [ ] Keep `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` in sync — if a rule changes here, check whether CLAUDE.md's "why" context needs updating too.

